# What does NOT travel in `git archive`, and therefore not in the delivery zip.
#
# The repository keeps everything — the working history is useful to whoever
# works here. What gets excluded is excluded from the package the examiner
# receives, which is code, data, and what explains them.
#
# Build the zip with `scripts/empacotar_entrega.sh`, which honours this file and
# also adds `data/` (which git ignores) without its 247 MB cache.

# ---- THE .md RULE: none of them travel, EXCEPT the READMEs ----
#
# By blanket exclusion and explicit re-opening, not by a list of names. A list
# protects against what already exists; this protects against the next file
# somebody adds without remembering to exclude it — which is how these things
# escape.
#
# `-export-ignore` unsets the attribute set by the line above, and is the only
# way to carve out an exception in gitattributes.
*.md                export-ignore
README.md           -export-ignore
**/README.md        -export-ignore

# ---- docs/ ----
# Implementation specs and architecture decisions, written during the
# experimental phase and annotated where they were superseded. Whatever still
# matters from them to whoever receives the package was moved into
# `scripts/README.md`, which is written to be read from the outside.
docs/               export-ignore

# ---- Tooling for whoever prepares the delivery ----
# The packager is of no use to whoever receives the package — it serves the
# person building it.
scripts/empacotar_entrega.sh  export-ignore
